<a id="interview-prep"></a>
🎤 Interview prep
Try answering each question aloud before expanding it.
<details>
<summary><strong>1. What is DevOps?</strong></summary>

DevOps combines practices that help development and operations teams build, release, and operate software reliably. It emphasises shared responsibility, automation, and feedback.
</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>2. Is GitHub the same as Git?</strong></summary>

No. Git is a distributed version control system. GitHub hosts Git repositories and provides collaboration features such as pull requests and reviews.
</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>3. How do continuous delivery and deployment differ?</strong></summary>

Continuous delivery keeps validated changes ready to release, with a human production-release decision possible. Continuous deployment releases qualifying changes automatically after the required checks pass.
</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>4. What happens when a required CI test fails?</strong></summary>

The pipeline should report the failure and block promotion. Investigate the cause, fix it, and rerun the checks rather than routinely bypassing them.
</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>5. What is a build artifact?</strong></summary>

An output produced by a build that can be stored, tested, or deployed, such as a React build folder or a container image.
</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>6. Why does an application work locally but fail on a server?</strong></summary>

Dependencies, runtime versions, environment variables, permissions, or network access may differ. Start with logs and compare the environments systematically.
</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>7. How are Vagrant and a VM provider different?</strong></summary>

Vagrant describes and manages VM environments. The provider supplies the underlying capability to run the virtual machines.
</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>8. Does an AWS budget alert automatically stop spending?</strong></summary>

No. Notifications can lag and are not a guaranteed spending cap. Check usage and remove unneeded resources after labs.
</details>

